      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Picoas_station"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The station opened on 29 December 1959 as part of the original Lisbon Metro network.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Picoas_station"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The original station design was created by architect Falcão e Cunha.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Picoas_station"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1982 the station was extended, with the new layout designed by Benoliel de Carvalho.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Picoas_station"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A 1995 refurbishment introduced a fresh look by architect Dinis Gomes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Picoas_station"
    },
    {
